.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rars-add 1 "" rars
.SH NAME
rars\-add \- Create a new archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrars add\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-store\fR] [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-dict\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-memory\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-memory\fR] [\fB\-\-temp\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-solid\fR] [\fB\-\-encrypt\-headers\fR] [\fB\-\-quick\-open\fR] [\fB\-\-blake2sp\fR] [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-\-archive\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-file\-comment\fR] [\fB\-\-recovery\-percent\fR] [\fB\-\-volume\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-delta\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-e8\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-e8e9\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-itanium\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-rgb\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-audio\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-arm\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-ppmd\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-base\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIARCHIVE\fR> <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new archive
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
Archive password (visible in process list \[u2014] prefer \-\-password\-file or the TTY prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads for parallel compression and extraction (default: all available cores)
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read password from file ("\-" for stdin); trailing newlines are stripped
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting mode for long\-running operations
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: rar50]
Target archive format (default: rar50, the modern widely\-compatible format)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rar14
.IP \(bu 2
rar15
.IP \(bu 2
rar20
.IP \(bu 2
rar29
.IP \(bu 2
rar30
.IP \(bu 2
rar40
.IP \(bu 2
rar50
.IP \(bu 2
rar70
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-store\fR
Store files without compression (equivalent to \-\-level 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Compression level (0..5; 0 implies \-\-store)
.TP
\fB\-\-dict\-size\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Dictionary size (e.g. 4m, 128k; RAR 1.5+)

Left unset, the writer fits one to the data: the smallest size that reaches across the largest member, or the whole archive when \-\-solid shares one window. A larger dictionary can pack better and always costs time and memory to search.
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\-limit\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum total compression working memory (default: 283m, plus 160m per thread past the first, up to a quarter of RAM or the cgroup limit on Linux)

At 283m or above, the budget only affects how much work runs at once. Below 283m it can also change the archive by planning smaller jobs.

Left unset rather than defaulted here, so a volume set below RAR 5, which is still built in memory, can tell an explicit request from a default and refuse the one it cannot honour.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-memory\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Hard managed\-allocation ceiling for RAR5/7, separate from estimated workspace
.TP
\fB\-\-temp\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Directory for temporary compressed payloads (RAR 5+)
.TP
\fB\-\-solid\fR
Use solid compression (treats inputs as one continuous stream)
.TP
\fB\-\-encrypt\-headers\fR
Encrypt archive headers (RAR 3.x/4.x and RAR 5+) (requires \-\-password)
.TP
\fB\-\-quick\-open\fR
Emit a quick\-open service block (RAR 5+ only)
.TP
\fB\-\-blake2sp\fR
Store a BLAKE2sp hash of each file beside its CRC32 (RAR 5+ only)
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Archive\-level comment
.TP
\fB\-\-archive\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Archive name to embed in archive metadata service (RAR 5+)
.TP
\fB\-\-file\-comment\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Per\-file comment (not RAR 3.x/4.x)
.TP
\fB\-\-recovery\-percent\fR \fI<PERCENT>\fR
Add a recovery record at the given percentage (1..100; RAR 5+)
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\-size\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Split archive into volumes of this size
.TP
\fB\-\-delta\-filter\fR \fI<CHANNELS>\fR
Delta filter with the given channel count (RAR 2.9+)
.TP
\fB\-\-e8\-filter\fR
E8 x86 call filter (RAR 2.9+)
.TP
\fB\-\-e8e9\-filter\fR
E8E9 x86 call/jump filter (RAR 2.9+)
.TP
\fB\-\-itanium\-filter\fR
Itanium filter (RAR 2.9/3.x/4.x only)
.TP
\fB\-\-rgb\-filter\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR
RGB image filter with the given pixel width (RAR 2.9/3.x/4.x only)
.TP
\fB\-\-audio\-filter\fR \fI<CHANNELS>\fR
Audio filter with the given channel count (RAR 2.9/3.x/4.x only)
.TP
\fB\-\-arm\-filter\fR
ARM filter (RAR 5+ only)
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-filter\fR
Auto\-detect data filter (RAR 5+ does this by default)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-filter\fR
Skip filter detection, compressing the data as it is (RAR 2.9+; the older formats never look, so the flag passes without comment there)
.TP
\fB\-\-ppmd\fR
Use the PPMd compression algorithm (RAR 2.9/3.x/4.x only)

Cannot be combined with \-\-auto\-filter: choosing a filter means measuring candidates through LZ, which forcing PPMd leaves nothing to measure.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-base\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Read inputs from this directory and store names relative to it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIARCHIVE\fR>
Output archive path
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Files (and directories) to add to the archive
